messages:
sam_cs: Quick sync request — Orbit dedicated bring-up tomorrow 09:30 PT. Quota approved but we still need autoscale params, loadtest windows, and an enablement plan. CC @leo_infra @jin_prod @tara_oncall
leo_infra: I can join. drop the expected RPS profile + tail latency SLO and I'll sketch autoscale options
jin_prod: Quick notes — expected steady ~150 rps, burst to ~450 rps for short periods. Target 95th latency <= 150ms. Quota = 1.2M tokens/day.
sam_cs: thanks. short config we're proposing:
```
reserved_pool: 2xA100
burst_pool: 4xA100 (auto-burst)
quota: 1200000 tokens/day
latency_slo: p95 <= 150ms
```
jin_prod: Autoscale suggestion: min_instances: 2, max_instances: 12, scale_metric: gpu_util, target_util: 70%. Also enable prefix caching for prompt templates to cut token compute on common paths.
tara_oncall: We're planning a 30m soak + burst test tomorrow 10:00 PT. Who can drop the k6/locust snippet? I can kick off and monitor traces.
sam_cs: minimal k6 snippet you can use (replace token):
```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
export default function() {
  const res = http.post('https://api.redwood.example/v1/generate', JSON.stringify({input: 'loadtest'}), { 
    headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer TEST_TOKEN', 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }
  });
  sleep(1);
}
```
opsbot: loadtest job created: staging/orbit-bringup | start=2025-03-15T17:00Z | duration=00:30:00 | owner=tara_oncall
nisha_pm: Heads-up — renewal risk flag: Orbit usage growth slower than forecast. Post-test we should send the enablement playbook and set a joint customer call. I can own the customer readiness check Thurs EOD.
sam_cs: Action items: 1) leo tune autoscale and add queue-based fallback; 2) jin provide cache whitelist + model-variant fallbacks; 3) tara run soak and post metrics in thread; 4) nisha schedule enablement + customer call. I'll update the runbook and push the canary policy.
leo_infra: on it. I'll add fallback routing: if avg_queue_ms > 200 then route to compact-variant and open an incident ticket automatically.
sam_cs: perfect, thanks everyone :thumbsup:
